  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zimbabwe Lawyers for Human Rights.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The expected results of the Project are as follows:
Impact: Protection of human rights and the 2013 Constitution

Outcome 1: Sustained access to legal support by human rights defenders. 
Output 1.1. Human Rights Defenders protection bolstered  
Output 1.2 HRDs continue with their work

Outcome 2: Constitutional Rights enforced and Protected
Output 2.1 Accountability for violations of the constitution
Output 2.2. Lawyers litigation skills enhanced/Forums symposiums/strategic meetings needed. 

Outcome 3: Improved knowledge for targeted evidence-based responses by policy makers
Output 3.1 Evidence-based informed action/responses to human rights issues.
Output 3.2 Evidence Based research on civic space
Output 3.2 Increased understanding awareness of human rights issues

Outcome 4: Institutional Strengthening
Output 4.1. Enhanced ZLHR Institutional Capacity	
Output 4.2 Reinforced Security mechanisms for ZLHR &amp; its key staff</narrative>
  </description>
